# Backlog

This directory is managed by **VAT** (Versioned Addressable Tasks) — a tiny
command-line tool for capturing a project's backlog as plain markdown, kept
right next to the code.

## Install

```sh
cargo install --git https://github.com/jmbeach/vat
```

Tagged releases also carry prebuilt binaries — see the
[Releases page](https://github.com/jmbeach/vat/releases).

## Files

- `backlog.md` — the flat list of tasks. Jot one-line `-` bullets here as you
  think of them; `vat sync` later gives each a stable ID.
- `vat.toml` — project config. Holds the 3-char ID prefix for this repo:
  `{prefix}`.
- `.used-ids` — tombstone list of every ID ever issued. Committed so a deleted
  task's ID is never handed out again. Don't hand-edit.
- `items/<id>.md` — per-task notes. Created when a task has notes, deleted when
  the task is marked done.
- `README.md` — this file. Written once by `vat init`; VAT never reads or
  rewrites it afterward, so edit or delete it freely.

## Workflow

1. Jot new bullets into `backlog.md`:

   ```
   - rewrite the cache layer
       why: the LRU is thrashing on hot keys
   ```

2. Run `vat sync` to assign each new bullet a stable ID (e.g. `{prefix}-7k2`)
   and tuck any indented notes into `items/<id>.md`.
3. Claim a task with `vat start {prefix}-7k2`.
4. Finish it with `vat done {prefix}-7k2` — the bullet is removed from
   `backlog.md` and its ID is tombstoned in `.used-ids`.
